{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And at the end appeared:</b> — the meaning is 'their whole appearance.' The Gaon [Saadia] said: this was a great miracle, and there is no need [for natural explanation], for they were eating rice, called in Arabic ארוז, and it is very esteemed and sweeter than wheat and produces pure blood, and it is the food of the people of India, and they have no wheat, and dishes were made from it. And this rice swells greatly when cooked in milk. And the general principle is that a little of it satisfies, and it is heavy in its weight, and its grains are very fine and not round, and its nature is hot and moist. And the wonder is [coming] from a great sage who said that it is דוחן (millet), whose grains are round and which lasts many years without rotting, and it is a bad food and its nature is cold and dry. Also among legumes, אפונים (chickpeas) — and these are not those found in France, for those are cold and bad and cause flatulence, whereas the אפונים are found in Spain, Egypt, Rome, and Provence, and they are of three types: white, red, and black, and this species is the most esteemed of all. And all three types are hot and moist, and their liquid is a remedy for the liver, and they gladden the face more than wine. And a person can distinguish, for those of France have no 'mouth,' whereas the three types do have 'mouth.' Now rice and chickpeas are seed-foods and fatten the flesh. Furthermore, any food that the soul desires benefits more than food the soul does not love, even if the latter be hot and moist like the nature of life — and behold, these were eating something their souls desired, and it benefited them."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:04.370336271Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}